[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807535474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115477#issuecomment-3807535474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115477","id":3807535474,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i8mFy","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T21:06:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T21:06:34Z","body":"One potential fix might be to just add handlers for the improperly flushed messages to `RemoteDebugger::_core_capture`, but I feel like the fundamental problem here is that we're executing GDScript while debugging GDScript. I have to assume that's not desirable.\n\nAt the very least we shouldn't be flushing anything from `RemoteDebugger::poll_events` if `RemoteDebugger::debug` is already on the stack.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807535474/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/r