":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T19:31:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T19:34:35Z","body":"> This might be related to lower stack size on macOS IIRC\n\nIt's not a crash or anything like that. The problem is with debugger messages being discarded.\n\nThere might still be some more macOS-specific change we can make, but I would guess that other platforms would exhibit the same problem if/when they move to using something similar to `DisplayServerEmbedded`/`EmbeddedDebugger`.\n\nI put up a pull request (#115532) for the change I mentioned above, about preventing `RemoteDebugger::poll_events` from running at all during a debugger break. It's a bit crude perhaps, but seems to do the trick.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813445536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]